 appropriate cir- cumstances to restrain an employee from violating express or implied con- tractual obligations. This includes em- ployees who are under an implied con- tractual duty of loyalty under § 8.01(a) or employees who have entered into reasonable restrictive covenants (§§ 8.06–8.08). . . . Recitals in agree- ments stipulating satisfaction of such requirements are given weight but are not determinative of whether the court should issue an injunction. . . . § 9.08 RESTATEMENT OF EMPLOYMENT LAW"